  <h2 class="section-title">Static Gear Engine Box · Side View + Top-Down View · Full Detail</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The static gear engine box is the heart of the Miasma Decker 9000. Two steam-driven pistons each drive one side
    of the box via crosshead-guided piston rods connecting to rails on the wheels. Three cross shafts with synchronizing gears
    ensure all six wheels rotate together. The front output shaft passes through a bevel gear to drive the generator chain.
    The rear output shaft exits to the transmission.
  </p>

